---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Niko Beutler and this blog.">
  <div class="narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Hi, I’m Niko. I work in IT infrastructure and have kept this blog since 2014 – mostly as a notebook for
        myself, and hopefully useful to whoever lands here from a search engine.
      </p>
      <p>
        The early posts are about VMware vSphere and Horizon, PowerShell and PowerCLI, and running my own Linux web
        and mail servers. Later it moved on to Azure, Azure Virtual Desktop and the Power Platform. In between there
        was the occasional FPV quadcopter build.
      </p>
      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Find me on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>. Legal details are in the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        Since October 2026 this site is <strong>built and maintained by AI</strong> – Claude by Anthropic, working with
        me. It writes the code, drafts posts from my input, and I review everything before it goes live. Each post is
        labeled with who wrote it. The details are on the <a href="/ai/">AI page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technically it’s a static site built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on GitHub Pages.
        No cookies, no tracking, no comments. The old WordPress posts were restored from the
        <a href="https://web.archive.org/">Internet Archive</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
